<title>DENMARK: SAS inaugurates new Stockholm-Russia route.</title>
<headline>SAS inaugurates new Stockholm-Russia route.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS) said in Monday it inaugurated a new non-stop three-times weekly scheduled route between Stockholm and Arkhangelsk, north Russia.</p>
<p>The route is SAS' fourth Russian destination, the others being from Stockholm and Copenhagen to Moscow and St. Petersburg and from Copenhagen to Kaliningrad.</p>
<p>&quot;SAS sees Archangelsk as an important destination for Scandinavian as well as European and American business,&quot; the airline wrote in a statement.</p>
<p>--Chjris Follett, Copenhagen newsropom +45-33 969652</p>
